  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), す-row.\n- Negative: {根|ね}ざさない\n- Polite: {根|ね}ざします\n- Te-form: {根|ね}ざして\n- Past: {根|ね}ざした\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n〜に{根|ね}ざす: to be rooted in ~\nThe past participle form 〜に{根|ね}ざした is extremely common as a modifier (e.g., {地域|ちいき}に{根|ね}ざした — rooted in the community).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{根付|ねづ}く (to take root) describes the process of becoming established. {根|ね}ざす describes the state of being rooted in something, emphasizing the deep origin or basis.",
